                <pb facs="0540" n="475" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg475"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.11241/34</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2591</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-09">March 9, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        20.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    Instruction No. 1173 of January 17, 1936, with respect to customs privileges for
                    American educational and philanthropic institutions in Syria, I have the honor
                    to report that this entire matter has the earnest attention of the Embassy.</p>
                <p>Since the receipt of the Department’s Instruction under acknowledgement, renewed
                    formal and informal representations have been made to the Foreign Office, and
                    this morning, Mr. Marriner, Counselor of the Embassy, had occasion to discuss
                    the question with M. Chauvel of the Africa-Levant Division of the Ministry for
                    Foreign Affairs. A copy of a memorandum of their conversation is transmitted
                    herewith. Mr. Marriner expects to meet M. de Martel, the French High
                    Commissioner, who is due in Paris toward the end of this month and will at that
                    time endeavor to hasten a satisfactory settlement of the matter of customs
                    immunity for American institutions in Syria.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jesse Isidor
                    Straus</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d544-a1.xml" xpointer="d544-a1"/>
